Status: 4 of 4 initial reports + 7 follow-up sub-agent reports + 1 NSIS skeleton. All under 256 lines. Top-line findings: mingw-w64 MSVCRT for Phase 1 cross-compile (UCRT is NOT installed on this host - corrected after user caught a wrong UCRT claim); 86/95 chs_rt POSIX sites have direct Windows equivalents; 9 need redesign (Landlock → Job Object + restricted token + NTFS DACL; RLIMIT_NOFILE → no-op; the rest narrow shims); the compiler source is portable but 3 shell invocations in 4 files need a `process_target` table; NSIS for the Windows installer.

## Build-test result (orchestrator, 2026-08-19 07:45)

The orchestrator ran an end-to-end build test on this host. Real results, not predictions:

1. **Empty C + mingw → valid PE32+ .exe** ✓
2. **C with `printf` + mingw → valid PE32+ .exe** ✓
3. **C with `#include <windows.h>` + mingw → valid PE32+ .exe** ✓
4. **`oodac emit-c fixtures/hello.oo` → 214-line C file** ✓
5. **The 214-line C + mingw (no chs_rt link) → `x86-64 COFF object file, 11 sections, 63 symbols`** ✓ — **the C emit is fully cross-compile-clean.**
6. **The 214-line C + chs_rt.c + mingw → fails at chs_rt_sys.c:4 `fatal error: sys/wait.h: No such file or directory`** — the chs_rt runtime includes Linux-only headers.
7. **Stub-replacing chs_rt and linking → fails at link with undefined references to `oo_str_lit`, `oo_str_concat`, `oo_str_eq`, `oo_str_release`** — these are the runtime functions the chs_rt port must provide.

**Net finding:** The C emit is 100% portable to mingw. The chs_rt runtime is the ONLY blocker. Phase 2 (chs_rt Windows port) is the gate before any `.exe` can run.

## Survey correction (the UCRT error was a real error)

An earlier draft of `win_toolchain_survey.oot` claimed UCRT was the default. The user caught the error. The corrected survey documents: mingw64-gcc **MSVCRT** is installed at `/usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc` (16.1.1-1.fc44). UCRT is not installed. The C emit + MSVCRT chain works for empty C, C+printf, and C+windows.h.

