- [x] `audit/win_c_emit_compat.oot` (sub-agent I). The C emitter is 90% likely to compile under mingw with a chs_rt shim. Top 3 risks: (1) fork/setrlimit/prctl, (2) pthread link, (3) `sh -c` literal in process_exec. The build script (bash) and `nm` check are 0% portable and need separate work.
- [x] `audit/win_chs_rt_audit_2nd.oot` (sub-agent J). Second-opinion audit of B. Found 3 material misses: (1) `chs_rt_wasm.c:161` `fopen("/proc/self/cmdline", "rb")` — same /proc path B caught in chs_rt_sys.c:158 but in a different file, the wasm builder will fail on Windows if the shim only covers chs_rt_sys.c. (2) `chs_rt_vision.c:209,210,228,229` four `mkdir(".ooda-cache", 0755)` calls — direct Windows equivalents (CreateDirectoryA), not redesigns. (3) `chs_rt_landlock.c:43` `__attribute__((packed))` — portable under mingw-w64 GCC, but B should have noted it. Also: B said 9 redesigns in §5, but §4 has 11; B's §5 is the typo.
